{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=4$ and $‖3u+2v‖=17.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $3u$ is orthogonal to $2v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖3u{‖}^{2}+‖2v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =(3‖u‖)^{2}+(2‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (17)^{2} & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4(4)^{2} \\\\ 289 & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4\\cdot 16 \\\\ 289 & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+64 \\\\ 225 & =9‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-74106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=15$ and $‖u+\\sqrt{5}v‖=75.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{5}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5}‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (75)^{2} & =(15)^{2}+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,625 & =225+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,400 & =5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =1\\,080\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=6\\sqrt{30}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-40264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "32"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{41}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{30}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{1\\,013}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\sqrt{30}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=4$ and $‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v‖=\\sqrt{182}.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $\\sqrt{2}u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{3}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =‖\\sqrt{2}u{‖}^{2}+‖\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{2}‖u‖)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =2‖u{‖}^{2}+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (\\sqrt{182})^{2} & =2(4)^{2}+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 182 & =2\\cdot 16+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 182 & =32+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 150 & =3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=5\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-74109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=6\\sqrt{2}$ and $‖u+2v‖=6\\sqrt{6}.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $u$ is orthogonal to $2v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖2v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u‖+(‖2v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (6\\sqrt{6})^{2} & =(6\\sqrt{2})^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 216 & =72+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 144 & =4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=7$ and $‖2u+v‖=25.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $2u$ is orthogonal to $v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =‖2u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =(2‖u‖)^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+(7)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+49 \\\\ 576 & =4‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\sqrt{12}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{337}{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $‖u+5v‖=19$ and $‖u‖=4$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+5v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+‖5v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+5v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+5‖v‖ \\\\ 19 & \\le 4+5‖v‖ \\\\ 15 & \\le 5‖v‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74177" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-74177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74177" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $‖5u-4v‖=26$ and $‖u‖=2$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖5u-4v‖ & \\le ‖5u‖+‖-4v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖5u-4v‖ & \\le 5‖u‖+4‖v‖ \\\\ 26 & \\le 5\\cdot 2+4‖v‖ \\\\ 26 & \\le 10+4‖v‖ \\\\ 16 & \\le 4‖v‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-140459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json