n\\begin{aligned}‖4u+v‖ & \\le 4‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 29 & \\le 4‖u‖+5 \\\\ 24 & \\le 4‖u‖ \\\\ 6 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-40899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $‖8u-v‖=35$ and $‖v‖=11$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖8u-v‖ & \\le ‖8u‖+‖-v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖8u-v‖ & \\le 8‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 35 & \\le 8‖u‖+11 \\\\ 24 & \\le 8‖u‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-140460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2}=50$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=4$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =17‖v{‖}^{2}+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & \\le 17‖v‖+16 \\\\ 34 & \\le 17‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $2\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{2}\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=19$ and $‖v‖=9$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (9)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =9‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 9‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =9‖u‖+(‖u‖+9) \\\\  & =10‖u‖+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19 & \\le 10‖u‖+9 \\\\ 10 & \\le 10‖u‖ \\\\ 1 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-40243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-40243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=39$ and $‖v‖=7$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}39 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (7)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =7‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 7‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =7‖u‖+(‖u‖+7) \\\\  & =8‖u‖+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}39 & \\le 8‖u‖+7 \\\\ 32 & \\le 8‖u‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-140461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{39}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-140461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=34$ and $‖v‖=6$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}34 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (6)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =6‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 6‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =6‖u‖+(‖u‖+6) \\\\  & =7‖u‖+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}34 & \\le 7‖u‖+6 \\\\ 28 & \\le 7‖u‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-39608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-39608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2}=62$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=3$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}62 & ={|u\\cdot v|}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4(‖v{‖}^{2}+{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =13‖v{‖}^{2}+36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}62 & \\le 13‖v{‖}^{2}+36 \\\\ 26 & \\le 13‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $2\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{2}\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6297f9e56cb57b1d79f5f50f4f410d895cc53b635661ae753c51f260a8a7e2bc"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "da8a09eff646e98f08bc791332292fbef43ae66c6e0ae0ba29d8753ba9f1a921"} {"question" "e-5557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ be vectors such that $\\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert = 6$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{u}+4\\mathbf{v} \\Vert = 25.$  If $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v},$ find $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5557.json" "file_sha256" "e28fb05018f3a3fabd681b35e62b244f9f05c85e73d4defb1a40fb653cb50912"} {"question" "e-5557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v},$ we also have that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $4\\mathbf{v}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+4v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖4v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+4v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+(4‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+4v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+16‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+16(6)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =‖u{‖}^{2}+576 \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =625-576 \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}=\\Vert\\mathbf{u}\\Vert^2=49.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5557.json" "file_sha256" "e28fb05018f3a3fabd681b35e62b244f9f05c85e73d4defb1a40fb653cb50912"} {"question" "e-5558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} +3\\mathbf{v} \\Vert=14$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert=2,$ find the smallest possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u}\\Vert.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5558.json" "file_sha256" "4550c6565ad8b32377202ea4bb30fa13f99ced37d37012c40a0c9e58ccf49057"} {"question" "e-5558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+3v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+‖3v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+3v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+3‖v‖ \\\\ 14 & \\le ‖u‖+3(2) \\\\ 14 & \\le ‖u‖+6 \\\\ 8 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ is $8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5558.json" "file_sha256" "4550c6565ad8b32377202ea4bb30fa13f99ced37d37012c40a0c9e58ccf49057"} {"question" "e-5559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let the vectors $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}|^2+5\\Vert\\mathbf{v}+\\mathbf{w}\\Vert^2=29$ and $\\| \\mathbf{u} \\|  = \\| \\mathbf{w} \\| = 2$, then what is the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5559.json" "file_sha256" "62f3e1d27ad9ff46f5a1555ccf4a0a78819d10eac567ae52c2fe65417d47a5e4"} {"question" "e-5559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =4‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{w}$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =4‖v{‖}^{2}+5(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & \\le 4‖v{‖}^{2}+5(‖v{‖}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & \\le 9‖v{‖}^{2}+20 \\\\ 9 & \\le 9‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 1 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert^2$ implies that $1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$. Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$ is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5559.json" "file_sha256" "62f3e1d27ad9ff46f5a1555ccf4a0a78819d10eac567ae52c2fe65417d47a5e4"}] "usage" {"e-5559" [] "q-39412" [] "q-40244" [] "e-5558" [] "q-39610" [] "e-5557" []} "basis" 1466 "retractions" [[17592186134141 :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖ = 7$ and $‖2u + v‖ = 25$. If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖$."] [17592186134200 :question/problem "Given that $‖7u + v‖ = 32$ and $‖v‖ = 4$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$."] [17592186134150 :question/problem "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal.\n\nIf $\\mid u \\cdot v \\mid ^{2} + ‖v + w‖^{2} = 50$ and $‖u‖ = ‖w‖ = 4$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$?"] [17592186133505 :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ be vectors such that $\\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert = 6$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{u}+4\\mathbf{v} \\Vert = 25$. If $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$, find $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}$."] [17592186133505 :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$, we also have that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $4\\mathbf{v}$. So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖u + 4v‖^{2} &= ‖u‖^{2} + ‖4v‖^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖u + 4v‖^{2} &= ‖u‖^{2} + (4‖v‖)^{2} \\\\\n‖u + 4v‖^{2} &= ‖u‖^{2} + 16‖v‖^{2} \\\\\n(25)^{2} &= ‖u‖^{2} + 16(6)^{2} \\\\\n625 &= ‖u‖^{2} + 576 \\\\\n‖u‖^{2} &= 625 - 576 \\\\\n‖u‖^{2} &= 49\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}=\\Vert\\mathbf{u}\\Vert^2=49\n$$"] [17592186133506 :question/problem "Given that $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} +3\\mathbf{v} \\Vert=14$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert=2$, find the smallest possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u}\\Vert$."] [17592186133506 :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n‖u + 3v‖ \\mid \\le ‖u‖ + ‖3v‖\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}‖u + 3v‖ & \\le ‖u‖ + 3‖v‖ \\\\ 14 & \\le ‖u‖ + 3(2) \\\\ 14 & \\le ‖u‖ + 6 \\\\ 8 & \\le ‖u‖\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ is $8$."] [17592186133507 :question/problem "Let the vectors $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ be orthogonal.\nIf $\\mid \\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\mid ^2+5\\Vert\\mathbf{v}+\\mathbf{w}\\Vert^2=29$ and $\\| \\mathbf{u} \\| = \\| \\mathbf{w} \\| = 2$, then what is the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$?"] [17592186133507 :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n29 &= \\mid u \\cdot v \\mid ^{2} + 5‖v + w‖^{2} \\\\\n&\\le ‖u‖^{2} \\cdot ‖v‖^{2} + 5‖v + w‖^{2} \\\\\n&= 2^{2} \\cdot ‖v‖^{2} + 5‖v + w‖^{2} \\\\\n&= 4‖v‖^{2} + 5‖v + w‖^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{w}$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4‖v‖^{2} + 5‖v + w‖^{2} &= 4‖v‖^{2} + 5(‖v‖^{2} + ‖w‖^{2}) \\\\\n&\\le 4‖v‖^{2} + 5(‖v‖^{2} + 2^{2}) \\\\\n&= 9‖v‖^{2} + 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}29 & \\le 9‖v‖^{2} + 20 \\\\ 9 & \\le 9‖v‖^{2} \\\\ 1 & \\le ‖v‖^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert^2\n$$\n\nimplies that\n\n$$\n1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert\n$$\n\n. Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$ is $1$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131289 17592186131290 17592186131291 17592186131292 17592186131293 17592186131343 17592186131344 17592186131345 17592186131346 17592186131347 17592186131643 17592186131644 17592186131645 17592186131646 17592186131647] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131288 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131288 :answer-field/id] [17592186131288 :answer-field/key] [17592186131288 :answer-field/type] [17592186131342 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131342 :answer-field/id] [17592186131342 :answer-field/key] [17592186131342 :answer-field/type] [17592186131642 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131642 :answer-field